<%= embed AppicaUI::SkeletonPreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
Skeleton(class: "h-4 w-40")
```

A low-level block with no size of its own - give it dimensions with utility classes (`h-*` / `w-*` / `size-*`) and
reshape it with `rounded-*` (it's `rounded-md` by default; `rounded-full` for a dot, `rounded-[inherit]` to match a
parent). Its surface and shimmer both come from `currentColor`, so a single `text-*` class recolors it, and
`effect:` picks the animation. Compose skeletons in the shape of the content they stand in for - a Turbo Frame's
placeholder, a lazy-loaded card - so nothing shifts when it arrives.

